Analysis: The first two nm commands show the memory location and the status of the files, that is they show in which memory location they are in, their address and the names under which they are being kept. Then comes the objdump command which is where the magic is visible, we can see that the last objdump is the longest and it  has a very straightforward explanation, ti’s because of the linking that has been done by the compiler that makes it be so long and final in contrast to the first two objdumps that are short and contain places where they keep the open space for the information to be stored once they are linked. Basically, we have two programs that were not compiled together so they have some pieces of code missing and they show where that missing code should be filled in. The final objdump already has the final and fully ready code in it.

